<dc:title>President&#039;s Park</dc:title>
<dc:description>President&#039;s Park is made up of the &lt;a href=&quot;http://mallhistory.org/items/show/66&quot;&gt;White House&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;http://mallhistory.org/items/show/315&quot;&gt;the Ellipse&lt;/a&gt;, and Lafayette Square, and has existed for more than 200 years. Originally, President&#039;s Park was only the grounds immediately surrounding the White House, but over time it grew to include Lafayette Square and the Ellipse. The Ellipse has been the site of the &lt;a href=&quot;http://mallhistory.org/items/show/524&quot;&gt;National Christmas Tree&lt;/a&gt; since 1923.</dc:description>
